  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "text": "Sticking to Google photos because I can search for my driving license just by searching 'license' or first 2-3 digits of my license number and it does it for me or search through photo captures of bills and documents by just entering partial Ids or any text the document might have like 'tax 2023'. I think its OCR and image search is what keeping me hostage there.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "source_id": "hn_40341455",
      "date": "2024-05-13",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "text_ocr_detection_failure"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "You could try Google Photos, it can now search text in images: . Disclaimer: I work at Google, though not on this product.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "source_id": "hn_21142958",
      "date": "2019-10-03",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "text_ocr_detection_failure"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "Honestly the most important feature for me is the search function where you can find text of objects in photos and the map+time search function I can't really ditch Google photos without these",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "source_id": "hn_37304218",
      "date": "2023-08-29",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "text_ocr_detection_failure"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "i use google photos for quick text based search, like me with clock tower or something. google photos can't maintain folder structure, so its always my 2nd backup. first one is miror in dropbox.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "source_id": "hn_38309764",
      "date": "2023-11-17",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "text_ocr_detection_failure"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "The new update is absolute wack, my photos aren't organized into different days anymore and everything is just bunched up. It's become almost impossible to find photos that I want since I like to document the things I do. very disappointed",
      "source": "Google Play Store",
      "source_id": "66eb94d8-9309-4476-825a-47dd0dd3941d",
      "date": "2026-07-17",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "text_ocr_detection_failure"
      ],
      "segment": "gen_x"
    }
  ],
